{
  vertexes: [
    {
      id: "1"
      L: Page
      P: {
        public: true
        fns: return { enabled: () => true }
        title: Tutorial - Store Tasks
        url: /tutorial
        key: StoreTasksTutorial
        props:
          '''return {
  isNoPermissionCheck: true
}'''
      }
    }
    {
      id: "2"
      L: Attr
      P: {
        css:
          '''return `._id {
  max-width: 800px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: ${args.theme.var.spacing?.lg || "2rem"};
  color: ${args.theme.var.color.text};
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  ._id {
    padding: ${args.theme.var.spacing?.md || "1rem"};
  }
}`;'''
        displayOrder: 1
        componentName: Html
        props:
          '''return {
  as: "div"
}'''
      }
    }
    {
      id: "3"
      L: Attr
      P: {
        css:
          '''return `._id {
  font-size: 2rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: ${args.theme.var.color.text};
  margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  ._id {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
  }
}`;'''
        displayOrder: 1
        componentName: Html
        props:
          '''return {
  as: "h1",
  text: "Tutorial"
}'''
      }
    }
    {
      id: "4"
      L: Attr
      P: {
        css:
          '''return `._id {
  font-size: 0.9375rem;
  line-height: 1.6;
  color: ${args.theme.var.color.muted};
  margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
}`;'''
        displayOrder: 2
        textType: markdown
        componentName: Html
        text: Follow these steps to get the most out of **Store Tasks**.
        props:
          '''return {
  as: "div",
}'''
      }
    }
    {
      id: "5"
      L: Attr
      P: {
        css: ""
        displayOrder: 3
        textType: markdown
        componentName: Html
        text:
          '''### 1. Install and open the app

Install **Store Tasks** from the [Shopify App Store](https://apps.shopify.com/). Open it from **Apps** in your Shopify admin so it loads in the embedded (iframe) experience.

### 2. Explore lists and tasks

Use the sidebar to switch between lists (or stay on **All tasks** depending on setup). Open **[Tasks](/tasks)** to manage rows in the table.

### 3. Create and edit tasks

Use **create** actions in the table to add rows. Fill in title, description, status, priority, optional due dates, assignee (staff), linked order, and comments.

### 4. Tune the table

Open **settings** when available to adjust columns—but **import/export** shortcuts may be hidden in some embedded setups.

### 5. Get help

Read [FAQ](/faq) and [Documentation](/docs); contact us from [Support](/support).
'''
        props:
          '''return {
  as: "div",
}'''
      }
    }
    {
      id: "6"
      L: PageLayout
      P: {
        componentName: ShopifyLayout
      }
    }
  ]
  edges: [
    { id: "e1", T: "Attr", S: "1", E: "2" }
    { id: "e2", T: "PageLayout", S: "1", E: "6" }
    { id: "e3", T: "Attr", S: "2", E: "3" }
    { id: "e4", T: "Attr", S: "2", E: "4" }
    { id: "e5", T: "Attr", S: "2", E: "5" }
  ]
}
